= Deployment prerequisites =

This repository is organized as MediaWiki source. Deployment must be '''non-destructive by default''' because V2 canon and the V1 provenance archive are intentionally separate.

== Required / assumed capabilities ==
* MediaWiki page/revision system
* Semantic MediaWiki for semantic properties and <code>#ask</code> queries
* CategoryTree where <code>&lt;categorytree&gt;</code> is used

== Portal namespace ==
<code>Portal:</code> is not a default MediaWiki namespace on every installation. V2 includes <code>Portal/</code> because BITwiki's historical design explicitly uses portals as high-level knowledge entry points.

Before import, either register a Portal namespace or deliberately map portal source while preserving intended public titles. Do not silently rename portal pages.

== Do not deploy the archive ==
<code>archive-v1/</code> is repository-only read-only provenance. It contains historical source/revision data and generated reports, not a second live wiki tree.

== Exact V1 preservation boundary ==
The exhaustive archive currently records 186 public pages / 606 revision bodies, all 9 live templates and callers, all 162 category memberships, all nonnegative namespace inventories and the maintenance reports required for migration validation.

A missing V2 file is therefore '''not''' permission to delete the corresponding live V1 page.

== Template safety ==
V1 <code>Template:Infobox</code> has 80 callers. Do not delete or replace it destructively until those callers have been migrated and verified.

The seven live decorative/header/footer templates still have callers. Archive status does not make them safe to remove; migrate callers first.

The 59 wanted templates are references to absent implementations. Do not create them automatically during deployment.

== Category safety ==
V1 uses 162 category names but has zero authored Category pages. V2 intentionally creates documented Category pages for selected canonical browse surfaces.

Do not copy all 162 labels into V2 as a flat taxonomy. Preserve the V1 membership archive and apply [[BITwiki:V1 category migration]].

== Safe migration ==
<pre>
1. refresh archive-v1 from the live public wiki
2. review archive-v1/audit.json
3. import/create reviewed V2 pages additively
4. verify rendering, transclusions, categories and semantic data
5. migrate each V1 source family / callers deliberately
6. move/merge/redirect only after source comparison
7. preserve revision history where technically possible
8. rerun maintenance reports and compare against the pre-migration snapshot
</pre>

== Required post-import checks ==
Review at minimum:
* [[Special:AllPages]]
* [[Special:UncategorizedPages]]
* [[Special:UncategorizedTemplates]]
* [[Special:UnusedTemplates]]
* [[Special:WantedTemplates]]
* [[Special:Categories]] / [[Special:WantedCategories]]
* [[Special:BrokenRedirects]] / [[Special:DoubleRedirects]]

A clean migration is not one with zero warnings at any cost. It is one where every remaining warning is understood and intentional.

